# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Security + caching headers for Cloudflare Pages.
# NO EFFECT on GitHub Pages — GitHub Pages cannot serve custom headers.
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build output root (dist/),
# where Vite copies it from public/.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is Report-Only: violations are logged to
# the browser console and reported to Sentry, nothing is blocked. After
# a clean week of normal use, rename it to Content-Security-Policy to
# enforce, and add: frame-ancestors 'none' (ignored in Report-Only mode,
# which is why it is left out below; X-Frame-Options covers framing
# until then).
#
# 'unsafe-inline' in script-src is required by legacy.js's inline
# onclick handlers; the origin allowlist still restricts where external
# scripts can load from.
#
# media-src 'self' blob: is required because Jarvis/breathwork voice
# fetches audio from the Jarvis Worker (/ops-speak) and plays it via
# new Audio(URL.createObjectURL(blob)). ElevenLabs itself is proxied
# server-side, so it never appears as a browser origin.
#
# connect-src also lists the script/style/font CDN hosts (www.gstatic.com,
# fonts.googleapis.com, fonts.gstatic.com, cdn.jsdelivr.net, www.youtube.com)
# even though those load via <script>/<link>. The service worker precaches
# and revalidates them with fetch() (sw.js PRECACHE_ASSETS + the
# stale-while-revalidate handler), and a fetch() from the SW is governed by
# connect-src, not script/style/font-src. Without them the SW's offline
# precache of the Firebase SDK, Tabler icons, and fonts fails under
# enforcement. Confirmed via Report-Only (sw.js:73 violations).
#
# HSTS is being ramped deliberately, each rung gated on the previous being
# stable: 300 (cutover) → 86400 = 1 day (CURRENT) → 2592000 = 30 days →
# 31536000 = 1 year + includeSubDomains. Stays apex-only (no
# includeSubDomains) until every *.centerpost.app subdomain is confirmed
# clean HTTPS — includeSubDomains with a long max-age is very sticky and
# hard to walk back.
#
# Cloudflare Pages JOINS duplicate header names with a comma (it does not
# let the most-specific path win), so Cache-Control is set per-path and
# is deliberately absent from /* — otherwise every asset would inherit a
# contradictory "no-cache, immutable".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.gstatic.com https://accounts.google.com https://www.youtube.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self' https://centerpost-jarvis.medicjth.workers.dev https://centerpost-guardian.medicjth.workers.dev https://centerpost-sentinel.medicjth.workers.dev https://centerpost-pulse.medicjth.workers.dev https://*.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com https://www.gstatic.com https://fonts.googleapis.com https://fonts.gstatic.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://www.youtube.com https://o4511667943505920.ingest.us.sentry.io; frame-src https://accounts.google.com https://www.youtube.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; report-uri https://o4511667943505920.ingest.us.sentry.io/api/4511668027129856/security/?sentry_key=fa11403c0d7a9449b1749d199dc90395

# Hashed, content-addressed build output. NOT immutable/long-cached, despite
# the filename hash normally making that safe: Cloudflare Pages answers ANY
# missing path under here with a 200 + index.html (its SPA fallback), not a
# 404 -- an asset that hasn't reached this edge yet mid-deploy, or a hashed
# filename that's rolled off since the last redeploy, gets that HTML back
# with a real 200 status. "immutable, max-age=31536000" told browsers to
# trust whatever they got under that URL for a year with no revalidation --
# so a browser unlucky enough to ask at exactly the wrong instant got stuck
# permanently serving index.html as its CSS (2026-08-23 report: Chrome
# broken, Safari fine, purely because of when each one asked). no-cache
# still lets browsers reuse the file via a fast conditional 304 (an ETag is
# already present) -- it just makes every load re-check with the edge
# instead of trusting a local copy unconditionally for a year. See sw.js's
# isPoisonedHTML for the matching guard in the service worker's own cache.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

# Non-hashed files the Service Worker relies on for update delivery —
# must always revalidate so a new deploy is picked up.
#
# The no-store is load-bearing, not redundant: this zone's Browser Cache
# TTL (Caching → Configuration, a separate setting from Cache Rules)
# rewrites a bare max-age/no-cache down to a fixed 4h (14400s) for
# browsers, but leaves no-store alone. Without it these files get cached
# for 4h and stale copies break update delivery. Do NOT simplify back to
# a bare "no-cache".
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
/legacy.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
/config.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
# /app.html was a stray Vite scaffold (deleted). Nothing links to /app, but
# both paths now fall through to the SPA 200+index.html fallback, so they
# still return HTML -- keep them no-store so a fallback response can never be
# cached under them. That caching is exactly what broke the site once before.
/app.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
/app
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
